:true,"_score_spread":54.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.1389348980870642,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":76.8,"_gate_incr_roic":0.27246575919905275,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.018013456251332965,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":27.3,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.2128738186032944,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0016845563472220036,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.00341,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Everus Construction Group, Inc. provides contracting services in the United States. It operates through two segments, Electrical & Mechanical and Transmission & Distribution. The Electrical & Mechanical segment provides construction and maintenance services of electrical and communication wiring, and infrastructure; fire suppression systems; and renewables infrastructure and mechanical piping services in public and private sectors. The Transmission & Distribution segment offers construction and maintenance of overhead and underground electrical, gas, and communication infrastructure and transportation related lighting, as well as design, manufacturing, and distribution of overhead and underground transmission line construction equipment and tools. It serves utilities, manufacturing, transportation, commercial, industrial, institutional, renewables, and governmental customers. The company was incorporated in 2024 and is headquartered in Bismarck, North Dakota. Everus Construction Group, Inc. was formerly a subsidiary of MDU Resources Group, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey S. Thiede | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $399K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $671 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Everus Construction Group, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $4.4B market cap on $3.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +31% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $90M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.78\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 12\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 39% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.39363218101867353},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 21% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Analyst Forecasts For Everus Construction Group, Inc. (NYSE:ECG) Are Surging Higher","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-ecg/everus-construction-group/news/analyst-forecasts-for-everus-construction-group-inc-nyseecg","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794477638.468,"orig